Content area from OpenRune/OpenRune-Server#353 (answers there: all of it, one PR per row, ids renumbered against main, wiki data is fine).

From our per-feature patches `44-jewellery-teleports`, `45-jewellery-charge-slot` (in [`openrune/upstream/`](https://github.com/AlexPerrin/osrs-plugins-reverse/tree/main/openrune/upstream) of osrs-plugins-reverse), on `main` (`c2492318d`).

**Problem.** Teleport jewellery did nothing.

**Change.** New module `content/travel/jewellery-teleports` + pack, for the games necklace, ring of dueling, amulet of glory, skills necklace and combat bracelet:
- Rub opens the teleport menu (interface 187 via script 217, with hotkeys, as RuneLite's Better Teleport Menu expects); worn destination ops teleport directly.
- Each use takes a charge with the OSRS messages ("Your games necklace has seven uses left.", "...crumbles to dust."); glory, skills necklace and combat bracelet keep an uncharged item.
- A charge swap replaces the item in place (45), so a worn necklace stays in the neck slot.

Server-only ids, numbered after the ids already on main and not shared with any of our other PRs, so they merge in any order: dbtables `jewellery_teleport_items` / `_dests` 56013-56014 (rows 60294-60350).

**Tests.** `JewelleryTeleportScriptTest` (integration). The charge-slot fix (45) was seen on a client first (a worn games necklace moved to the head slot).

On this branch (Docker `eclipse-temurin:21`, upstream's `./gradlew`, 4 GB container; a clean `freshCache` of main restored first, then `:or-cache:buildCache :or-cache:mergePluginGamevals`, then each task as a separate run, then `run` to "Server ready"): RESULTS_PENDING. `tools/scripts/fix_gameval_conflicts.py --check` finds no conflicts on this branch, nor with all of our open content PRs merged together.

Nothing was checked in game from this exact branch; the in-game checks above were on our own server build (an older main plus these and our other patches).

**Data sources.** OSRS Wiki (by the wiki's contributors, CC BY-NC-SA 3.0, https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/3.0/): destinations and their tiles, menu order and the charge messages (Games necklace, Ring of dueling, Amulet of glory, Skills necklace, Combat bracelet pages).

**Caveats.**
- Best guesses: the menu title, glory/skills/combat charge lines, the purple value, timing, and two planes (Corporeal Beast, Tears of Guthix).
- No destination requirements or landing radius.

**Release note.** Teleport jewellery works: Rub menu, worn ops and charges.

